%% Figure: Slack work-day bucketing with a configurable boundary hour
flowchart TB
    A["Slack message<br/>(epoch timestamp ts)"] --> B["Convert to local wall-clock<br/>in configured timezone (Asia/Kolkata)<br/>via Intl.DateTimeFormat"]
    B --> C{"local hour < <br/>day_boundary_hour (e.g. 6)?"}
    C -->|"yes"| D["work_date = previous calendar day<br/>(night shift stays whole)"]
    C -->|"no"| E["work_date = current calendar day"]
    D --> F["Classify message"]
    E --> F
    F --> G{"channel == attendance channel<br/>AND first message of work_date?"}
    G -->|"yes"| H["checked_in = true<br/>(check_in_time = ts)"]
    G -->|"no"| I{"channel name ends with<br/>work-update suffix?"}
    I -->|"yes"| J["posted_update = true"]
    I -->|"no"| K["was_active = true"]
    H --> L["UPSERT slack_daily_attendance<br/>(startup_id, user, work_date)"]
    J --> L
    K --> L
    L --> M["Today board reads CURRENT work_date<br/>by the wall clock — rolls over at boundary"]
